More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (251–260)
251. Insecure Cookie Configuration
Insecure Cookie Configuration
Cookies missing flags like Secure, HttpOnly, or SameSite, making them easier to steal.
💰 Typical payout: $100 – $1,500
252. Session Token in URL
Session Token Exposure
Session IDs appear in URLs, allowing attackers to capture them via logs or referrers.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
253. Password Reset via Username Only
Password Reset Vulnerability
Resetting passwords using only a username without proper verification.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
254. Improper Logout Handling
Improper Session Invalidation
Sessions remain active even after a user logs out.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
255. Referrer Header Data Leakage
Referrer Data Leakage
Sensitive information leaks through the HTTP referrer header.
💰 Typical payout: $100 – $2,000
256. Browser Cache Sensitive Data
Sensitive Data Stored in Browser Cache
Private data stored in browser cache accessible after logout.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
257. Hidden Parameter Manipulation
Hidden Parameter Manipulation
Hidden form fields modified by attackers to change application behavior.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $4,000
258. Improper Access to Logs
Log File Exposure
Application logs publicly accessible and contain sensitive information.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
259. API Debug Mode Enabled
API Debug Mode Exposure
APIs running in debug mode reveal internal system details.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
